Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 13:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kompakt: AOD straight from an awake display

primary_display_check_power_mode() reports DOZE only for an alive path
with the LCM in LCM_ON_LOW_POWER, and only the full resume set it. DOZE
requested while the path is alive (locking with the always-on display on,
no power-down first) took the DISP_ALIVE early exit, kept LCM_ON and left
the driver reporting FB_RESUME with meink in AOD. The early exit now marks
the LCM low power when the requested mode is DOZE, as mt6768's
primary_display_lcm_power_on_state() does. The Kompakt LCM is a
placeholder with an empty aod callback, so nothing is sent to a panel.

---
diff --git a/drivers/misc/mediatek/video/mt6765/videox/primary_display.c b/drivers/misc/mediatek/video/mt6765/videox/primary_display.c
--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/video/mt6765/videox/primary_display.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/video/mt6765/videox/primary_display.c
@@ -4935,6 +4935,17 @@
 			primary_display_set_lcm_power_state_nolock(LCM_ON);
 			DISPCHECK("kompakt-aod: forced LCM_ON on resume from DOZE\n");
 		}
+		/* Kompakt: DOZE straight from an awake path. The full resume that marks
+		 * the LCM low power is skipped, so mark it here, as mt6768 does.
+		 */
+		if (primary_display_get_power_mode_nolock() == DOZE &&
+			primary_display_get_lcm_power_state_nolock() !=
+			LCM_ON_LOW_POWER) {
+			if (pgc->plcm && pgc->plcm->drv && pgc->plcm->drv->aod)
+				disp_lcm_aod(pgc->plcm, 1);
+			primary_display_set_lcm_power_state_nolock(LCM_ON_LOW_POWER);
+			pr_info("kompakt-aod: DOZE from an awake path, LCM low power\n");
+		}
 		goto done;
 	}
 	mmprofile_log_ex(ddp_mmp_get_events()->primary_resume,
